HST Office: the English UI names the apps Sheets and Slides, never Calc or Impress.

The Vietnamese UI already says Sheets and Slides (l10n/vi-overrides.jsonl). Sixty-five English
source strings still named the engine's apps: tips of the day, extended tips, the Application
Colors entries "Calc Grid"/"Calc Text", the "Calc A1" formula syntax, the pivot-table source
"Data source registered in Calc", the Slides remote-control dialog, its menu command and the
Windows Start menu shortcut tooltips. They now use the short in-app names (Sheets, Slides), as
"%PRODUCTNAME Calc" does through the UI string hook. The remote-control download tooltip no
longer names the upstream app.

Every changed English string renames its Vietnamese entry via "msgid_new" in
l10n/vi-overrides.jsonl, so the translations still match.

Kept on purpose: the Bluetooth service record name of the remote-control server
(sd/source/ui/remotecontrol/BluetoothServiceRecord.hxx, protocol), filter and format names
("Calc MS Excel 2007 XML", StarCalc formats), UNO, .uno: and configuration identifiers, and the
legacy clipboard format names.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

